WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.629
The Implement phase is about putting the course into use.

2
00:00:03.629 --> 00:00:14.895
It includes publishing format decisions, LMS upload and configuration, learner access, launch testing, completion tracking, rollout communication, and support planning.

3
00:00:14.895 --> 00:00:18.071
Implementation is more than exporting a package.

4
00:00:18.071 --> 00:00:25.178
It is the operational work that ensures learners can actually launch, complete, and be credited for the course.

5
00:00:25.178 --> 00:00:28.807
Publishing format depends on the delivery environment.

6
00:00:28.807 --> 00:00:37.427
A SCORM package is commonly used when a course needs to communicate launch, progress, completion, score, or interaction data to an LMS.

7
00:00:37.427 --> 00:00:44.005
Other formats may be used for web delivery, internal portals, blended programs, or informal learning.

8
00:00:44.005 --> 00:00:49.297
The format should match the tracking and access requirements identified earlier.

9
00:00:49.297 --> 00:00:52.548
LMS configuration should be tested before launch.

10
00:00:52.548 --> 00:01:04.419
Confirm the course opens correctly, resumes as expected if resume is required, tracks completion, reports score if applicable, and behaves correctly for failed or passed assessments.

11
00:01:04.419 --> 00:01:09.712
Do not assume a package that works locally will behave the same way in the target LMS.

12
00:01:09.712 --> 00:01:12.963
Launch testing is part of implementation quality.

13
00:01:12.963 --> 00:01:15.987
Implementation also includes communication.

14
00:01:15.987 --> 00:01:24.229
Learners may need to know why the course matters, how long it takes, when it is due, how completion is tracked, and where to get help.

15
00:01:24.229 --> 00:01:27.026
Managers may need reporting expectations.

16
00:01:27.026 --> 00:01:34.511
Support teams may need answers for access problems, audio issues, browser questions, or completion discrepancies.

17
00:01:34.511 --> 00:01:36.402
Pilot groups can reduce risk.

18
00:01:36.402 --> 00:01:46.609
A small rollout can reveal confusing instructions, device issues, LMS behavior, missing support information, or content that does not land with the audience.

19
00:01:46.609 --> 00:01:54.397
Implementation succeeds when the course reaches learners reliably and the surrounding operation supports completion.
